codex
A more structural idea: for B=1, have the batched GEMM write the hidden dimension interleaved as `[N,N,H]`, so the final layernorm reads contiguous hidden vectors instead of strided `[H,N,N]`. I’m adding a separate output kernel to test whether the bmm store tradeoff is worth it.
